# Copy to api.conf and put your own machine's LAN address in it. api.conf is git-ignored,
# because it names one machine on one network and would be wrong for everyone else.
#
# Without it the launcher still builds and still writes its report to C:\Data\dump\ — you
# just have to fetch it over USB or Bluetooth, and read progress off the phone's screen
# rather than through `epoc logcat`.
#
# The address is where `epoc db serve` is listening. The device dials out to it; there is no
# discovery handshake in that direction, so this has to be right at build time.
#
#   ip addr | grep 'inet 192'      to find it on Linux
EPOCADB_HOST=192.168.0.10
